# M-package-manager step 3b (lane pm-fetch's finding, 2026-11-08): the
# program's catalogue reads the index `file://../idx`, and the catalogue of
# its package `json` reads `file://./../idx`, the same folder written another
# way. The build matched `json`'s entry for `text` to the program's by its
# source written as text, two texts, and refused the program, whose
# catalogue holds `text` (`heroes add` refused the same, `requirement_refused`).
# Each address is compared in its one form now, `file://../idx` for both, so
# `text` is one package and the program runs.
use <json>/parse

function main()
    print(parse.count("one index written two ways"))
